========================================================================================================================
VERDICT -- k04
========================================================================================================================
  d log a_0 / d log Upsilon = 1 + 2/ln(1/f_bar) for the closed-form inversion: 1.9 in the deep-MOND,
  dark-dominated regime where it was designed, but 4.9 at f_DM = 0.3 and 10.0 at f_DM = 0.2.
  The inversion is Upsilon-SAFE only where the dark-matter fraction is large.  Applied to baryon-
  dominated systems -- high-redshift discs, early-type galaxies inside R_e -- it is a mass-to-light
  meter with a_0's units.  This is a correction to the hunt's own vein A, found by differentiating
  its estimator, and it should be carried on every future use of the inversion.
